==Strategy==
The Two Cans can be blocked and killed quickly by [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cats]], they can do a few hits on Director Kurosawah before his attack wipes out everything. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] should be timed to hit the greatest amount of Two Cans as possible. Tanky cats are usually not recommended, as they will get the Two Cans to trigger their attack and hit the units that are not wave immune that are behind said tanky cat. Therefore, it is recommended to only use them if you are using ranged [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] cats, who make the stage fairly trivial anyways. Cat Machine in particular blows this stage out of the water due to it's high health (especially towards the Two Cans) and its wave-blocking properties, and allows the stage to be beaten with just [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and itself provided you cancel Director Kurosawah's first attack with the Cat Cannon and permafreeze him for the rest of the level.

Other units that can work include but are not limited to: [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], Talented [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] and other high DPS anti-Dark and generalist Rares/Super Rares.

For the {{4c}} stage, both [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Musashi]] and [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] can help you endure the wave attacks while whittling away at the Two Cans. Of course [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] can help due to his wave blocker trait but due to him getting knocked back frequently, it's not advised to use other backliners, especially if they are fragile, while trusting his ability to keep them safe. If you have unlocked [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] by this point in progression, you can spam him with 2 (Sm) Research [[Cat Combo]]s for an easy win.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|Anti-Dark]] Ubers - Naturally, as all the enemies here are Dark, anti-Dark Ubers do exceedingly well here. Ones with Wave Immunity, such as [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Keiji]], perform even better though.
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]] - Cat Machine Mk 3 is incredibly effective here, since he both resists and blocks the waves of the Two Cans. Cat Machine's only problem is that he does not resist Kurosawah.

